===Sales===
As of December 31, 2017, ''Super Mario Odyssey'' had sold 9.07 million copies worldwide, making it the best-selling game for the Nintendo Switch at the time.<ref>{{cite|url=https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ir/en/finance/software/index.html|archive=https://web.archive.org/web/20180131101811/https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ir/en/finance/software/index.html|date=December 31, 2017|deadlink=y|title=IR Information : Sales Data - Top Selling Title Sales Units|publisher=Nintendo|accessdate=July 16, 2026}}</ref> As of December 31, 2018, it reached 13.76 million copies, making it the best-selling 3D ''Super Mario'' game, although ''[[Mario Kart 8 Deluxe]]''{{'}}s 15.02 million copies lowered ''Super Mario Odyssey'' to the second-best-selling first-party game for the Nintendo Switch.<ref>{{cite|url=https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ir/en/finance/software/index.html|archive=https://web.archive.org/web/20190304002330/https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ir/en/finance/software/index.html|date=December 31, 2018|deadlink=y|title=IR Information : Sales Data - Top Selling Title Sales Units|publisher=Nintendo|accessdate=July 16, 2026}}</ref> As of September 30, 2026, the game had sold 31.06 million units worldwide, surpassing the sales of ''[[New Super Mario Bros.]]'' as the second best-selling ''Super Mario'' game. It is also the fifth best-selling first-party game for the Nintendo Switch.<ref>{{cite|url=https://www.nintendo.co.jp/ir/en/finance/software/switch.html|title=Top Selling Title Sales Units - Nintendo Switch Software|date=September 30, 2026|publisher=Nintendo|accessdate=November 5, 2026}}</ref>

